>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `SLOWSIMP_TAC`

``` hol4
clasimpLib.SLOWSIMP_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by non-committing depth-first search with simplification.

`SLOWSIMP_TAC thms` uses the classical slow search driver, which retains
unsafe alternatives after instantiating alternatives. Assumption-aware
full simplification from the current clasimpset is installed as an unsafe
wrapper on the current claset. Search is unbounded and can diverge.

Unmarked theorems are inserted as assumptions. Explicit classical markers,
`Simp`, `Iff`, and generic simplifier controls configure only this call.

### Failure

Fails unless search closes the goal. Search can diverge.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem slowsimp_tac_example:
  (p ==> q) ==> p ==> q
Proof
  clasimpLib.SLOWSIMP_TAC []
QED
```

